  "conclusions": [
    "The typed deontic converter plus deterministic decoder is the strongest primary path in this pilot.",
    "spaCy is useful as linguistic evidence but is not a semantic authority.",
    "Always-on raw spaCy evidence made Leanstral slower and less accurate.",
    "Leanstral fluency does not preserve prohibitions, permissions, condition scope, or temporal scope reliably enough for authoritative reverse translation.",
    "SyMAI is an orchestration layer over the same model and needs a reverse contract before round-trip evaluation.",
    "Hammer/cvc5 and Lean validate only supported non-vacuous formal identities; they cannot establish source-language correctness.",
    "Controlled CNL v2 is appropriate for simple restricted norms, not arbitrary multi-rule documents.",
    "The next ablation should test clause-level Leanstral repair only when the typed compiler reports a missing or low-confidence slot."
